Difference between a variable, array and a structure
•A variable can store only one value
•An array can store a number of variables of the same 
type
•A structure can store a number of variables of different 
type
-each element in a C structure is called member
•It is a good practice to initialize a structure to null 
while declaring, if we don’t assign any values to 
structure members
