Uses of union
•Union allows access to a common location by different data types, for 
example hardware input/output access, bitfield and word sharing, or type 
punning. Unions can also provide low -level polymorphism.
•Polymorphism is the ability of an object to take on many forms. 
•Type punning is a common term for any programming technique that 
subverts or circumvents or disrupts the type system of a programming 
language
•Type punning is a form of pointer aliasing where two pointers refer to the 
same location in memory but represent that location as different types
•Aliasing refers to the situation where the same memory location can be 
accessed using different names. 
•Unions provide an efficient way of using the same memory location for 
multiple -purpose.
